{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017F8D7Lk9xcMHcpVxSKnLn9","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (30KB). Full output saved to: /Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-batch-flvfok0r/30aafd76-3534-4666-ab29-0933a8953e34/tool-results/byh98t99m.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n=== config/tools.yaml\n     1\t# Tools per agent role, each with the task reason it is granted.\n     2\troles:\n     3\t  procurement:\n     4\t    tools:\n     5\t      read_document: \"Read vendor quotes, invoices and emails that arrived through the mail gateway.\"\n     6\t      extract_line_items: \"Delegate line-item extraction from long documents to the extractor.\"\n     7\t      get_budget: \"Check remaining department budget before raising a purchase order.\"\n     8\t      erp_call: \"Look up vendors, open invoices and purchase orders for matching.\"\n     9\t      create_purchase_order: \"Raise a purchase order once a quote is within budget and approved.\"\n    10\t      pay_invoice: \"Pay an invoice that is matched to a purchase order and approved.\"\n    11\t      post_slack_message: \"Ask staff for missing details and confirm orders with vendors.\"\n    12\t      memory_read: \"Recall department preferences and contract terms from earlier runs.\"\n    13\t      memory_write: \"Save new department preferences and contract terms.\"\n    14\t  extractor:\n    15\t    tools:\n    16\t      read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"\n=== app/extractor.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Line-item extraction sub-agent.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe parent procurement agent delegates structured extraction to a smaller\n     4\tmodel. The child runs under its own instance id, links to its parent in the\n     5\taudit graph, charges the parent's budget, and gets the extractor tool role.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport logging\n    11\tfrom typing import Any\n    12\t\n    13\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    14\t\n    15\tfrom app import audit\n    16\tfrom app.budget import Budget\n    17\tfrom app.context_size import measure_context\n    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    19\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n    20\tfrom app.tools import build_registry\n    21\t\n    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30aafd76-3534-4666-ab29-0933a8953e34","uuid":"f6852ed0-4211-4b82-9298-715fabd0748a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:27:06.822Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== config/tools.yaml\n     1\t# Tools per agent role, each with the task reason it is granted.\n     2\troles:\n     3\t  procurement:\n     4\t    tools:\n     5\t      read_document: \"Read vendor quotes, invoices and emails that arrived through the mail gateway.\"\n     6\t      extract_line_items: \"Delegate line-item extraction from long documents to the extractor.\"\n     7\t      get_budget: \"Check remaining department budget before raising a purchase order.\"\n     8\t      erp_call: \"Look up vendors, open invoices and purchase orders for matching.\"\n     9\t      create_purchase_order: \"Raise a purchase order once a quote is within budget and approved.\"\n    10\t      pay_invoice: \"Pay an invoice that is matched to a purchase order and approved.\"\n    11\t      post_slack_message: \"Ask staff for missing details and confirm orders with vendors.\"\n    12\t      memory_read: \"Recall department preferences and contract terms from earlier runs.\"\n    13\t      memory_write: \"Save new department preferences and contract terms.\"\n    14\t  extractor:\n    15\t    tools:\n    16\t      read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"\n=== app/extractor.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Line-item extraction sub-agent.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe parent procurement agent delegates structured extraction to a smaller\n     4\tmodel. The child runs under its own instance id, links to its parent in the\n     5\taudit graph, charges the parent's budget, and gets the extractor tool role.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport logging\n    11\tfrom typing import Any\n    12\t\n    13\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    14\t\n    15\tfrom app import audit\n    16\tfrom app.budget import Budget\n    17\tfrom app.context_size import measure_context\n    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    19\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n    20\tfrom app.tools import build_registry\n    21\t\n    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    23\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.extractor\")\n    24\t\n    25\tEXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"\n    26\tMAX_TURNS = 4\n    27\t\n    28\tLINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS = {\"sku\", \"description\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price_cents\", \"currency\"}\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tclass ExtractionFailed(Exception):\n    32\t    pass\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tclass LineItemExtractor:\n    36\t    def __init__(self, *, client, settings, deps, system_prompt: str):\n    37\t        self.client = client\n    38\t        self.settings = settings\n    39\t        self.deps = deps\n    40\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n    41\t\n    42\t    async def extract(self, parent: RunIdentity, doc_id: str, budget: Budget) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    43\t        budget.check_subagent()\n    44\t        ident = parent.child(role=EXTRACTOR_ROLE)\n    45\t        registry = build_registry(EXTRACTOR_ROLE, ident, self.deps)\n    46\t        task = f\"Extract every line item from document {doc_id}. Return JSON only.\"\n    47\t\n    48\t        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"gen_ai.invoke_agent line_item_extractor\") as span:\n    49\t            span.set_attribute(\"gen_ai.agent.id\", ident.agent_instance_id)\n    50\t            span.set_attribute(\"procurement.parent_instance_id\", parent.agent_instance_id)\n    51\t            start_node = await audit.record(\n    52\t                self.deps.pool,\n    53\t                ident,\n    54\t                kind=\"subagent_started\",\n    55\t                payload={\n    56\t                    \"role\": EXTRACTOR_ROLE,\n    57\t                    \"doc_id\": doc_id,\n    58\t                    \"parent_prompt_ref\": format(span.get_span_context().span_id, \"016x\"),\n    59\t                    \"tools\": registry.names(),\n    60\t                },\n    61\t            )\n    62\t\n    63\t            messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n    64\t            for _turn in range(MAX_TURNS):\n    65\t                budget.check_step()\n    66\t                request = {\n    67\t                    \"model\": self.settings.extractor_model_id,\n    68\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n    69\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n    70\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n    71\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n    72\t                }\n    73\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted=False)\n    74\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n    75\t                budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id, response.usage)\n    76\t                await budget.flush(self.deps.pool)\n    77\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n    78\t                decision = await audit.record(\n    79\t                    self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\n    80\t                    payload={\"requested_model\": request[\"model\"], \"served_model\": response.model,\n    81\t                             \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason},\n    82\t                )\n    83\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n    84\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n    85\t                if not uses:\n    86\t                    text = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n    87\t                    items = _parse_items(text)\n    88\t                    await audit.record(\n    89\t                        self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"subagent_finished\", parent=start_node,\n    90\t                        payload={\"items\": len(items)},\n    91\t                    )\n    92\t                    return items\n    93\t                results = []\n    94\t                for use in uses:\n    95\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n    96\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n    97\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n    98\t\n    99\t        raise ExtractionFailed(f\"no result after {MAX_TURNS} turns\")\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef _parse_items(text: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   103\t    try:\n   104\t        data = json.loads(text)\n   105\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n   106\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor returned non-JSON output\") from exc\n   107\t    if not isinstance(data, list) or len(data) > 500:\n   108\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor output must be a list of at most 500 items\")\n   109\t    items = []\n   110\t    for raw in data:\n   111\t        if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not set(raw) <= LINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS:\n   112\t            raise ExtractionFailed(\"unexpected line-item fields\")\n   113\t        items.append({k: redact_for_model(v) if isinstance(v, str) else v for k, v in raw.items()})\n   114\t    return items\n=== app/main.py\n     1\t\"\"\"FastAPI entry point for the procurement agent.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport asyncio\n     5\timport hashlib\n     6\timport hmac\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport logging\n     9\timport time\n    10\timport uuid\n    11\tfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n    12\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    13\tfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs\n    14\t\n    15\timport asyncpg\n    16\timport jwt\n    17\tfrom anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\n    18\tfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, HTTPException, Request\n    19\tfrom fastapi.security import HTTPAuthorizationCredentials, HTTPBearer\n    20\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    21\tfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n    22\t\n    23\tfrom app import audit, ingest\n    24\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore, ApproverNotAuthorized\n    25\tfrom app.extractor import LineItemExtractor\n    26\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n    27\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker, new_instance_id\n    28\tfrom app.loop import AgentDeps, ProcurementAgent\n    29\tfrom app.mcp_client import ErpMcpClient\n    30\tfrom app.redact import RedactingFilter\n    31\tfrom app.settings import get_settings\n    32\tfrom app.startup import startup_checks\n    33\tfrom app.tools.slack import SlackClient\n    34\t\n    35\tlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(asctime)s %(levelname)s %(name)s %(message)s\")\n    36\tfor handler in logging.getLogger().handlers:\n    37\t    handler.addFilter(RedactingFilter())\n    38\tlog = logging.getLogger(\"procurement\")\n    39\t\n    40\tAGENT_PRINCIPAL = \"spiffe://example-corp.test/ns/procurement-prod/sa/procurement-agent\"\n    41\tbearer = HTTPBearer()\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\tclass RunRequest(BaseModel):\n    45\t    task: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=4000)\n    46\t    department: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=64)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass Principal(BaseModel):\n    50\t    subject: str\n    51\t    business_unit: str\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef service_identity(settings, agent_type_id: str, tenant: str = \"system\") -> RunIdentity:\n    55\t    return RunIdentity(\n    56\t        accountable_party=\"system:procurement-agent\",\n    57\t        operational_owner=settings.operational_owner,\n    58\t        tenant=tenant,\n    59\t        agent_type_id=agent_type_id,\n    60\t        agent_instance_id=new_instance_id(),\n    61\t        trace_id=uuid.uuid4().hex,\n    62\t        run_id=f\"bg-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n    63\t        delegated_subject=\"system:procurement-agent\",\n    64\t        agent_principal=AGENT_PRINCIPAL,\n    65\t    )\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\tasync def expire_approvals_forever(app: FastAPI) -> None:\n    69\t    while True:\n    70\t        await asyncio.sleep(60)\n    71\t        ident = service_identity(app.state.settings, app.state.agent_type_id)\n    72\t        count = await app.state.pool.fetchval(\n    73\t            \"WITH e AS (UPDATE approvals SET status = 'expired' \"\n    74\t            \"WHERE status = 'pending' AND expires_at <= now() RETURNING 1) SELECT count(*) FROM e\"\n    75\t        )\n    76\t        await audit.record(app.state.pool, ident, kind=\"background_job\",\n    77\t                           payload={\"job\": \"expire_approvals\", \"expired\": count})\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t@asynccontextmanager\n    81\tasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    82\t    settings = get_settings()\n    83\t    agent_type_id = startup_checks(settings)\n    84\t    pool = await asyncpg.create_pool(settings.database_url, min_size=2, max_size=10)\n    85\t    broker = TokenBroker(settings)\n    86\t\n    87\t    async def slack_token() -> str:\n    88\t        return await broker.token_for(\"slack-proxy\", \"chat:write\", service_identity(settings, agent_type_id))\n    89\t\n    90\t    slack = SlackClient(settings.slack_api_url, slack_token)\n    91\t    approvals = ApprovalStore(pool, settings.policy, slack)\n    92\t    gate = PolicyGate(settings.policy, approvals)\n    93\t    erp = ErpMcpClient(settings.erp_mcp_url, settings.manifest[\"tool_pins\"], broker)\n    94\t    await erp.initialize(service_identity(settings, agent_type_id))\n    95\t\n    96\t    client = AsyncAnthropic()\n    97\t    deps = AgentDeps(settings=settings, pool=pool, gate=gate, erp=erp, slack=slack, broker=broker)\n    98\t    deps.extractor = LineItemExtractor(\n    99\t        client=client, settings=settings, deps=deps,\n   100\t        system_prompt=(settings.prompt_dir / \"extractor.md\").read_text(),\n   101\t    )\n   102\t    app.state.settings = settings\n   103\t    app.state.pool = pool\n   104\t    app.state.agent_type_id = agent_type_id\n   105\t    app.state.approvals = approvals\n   106\t    app.state.agent = ProcurementAgent(\n   107\t        client=client, deps=deps, system_prompt=(settings.prompt_dir / \"system.md\").read_text()\n   108\t    )\n   109\t    app.state.jwks = jwt.PyJWKClient(settings.oidc_jwks_url, cache_keys=True, lifespan=300)\n   110\t    sweeper = asyncio.create_task(expire_approvals_forever(app))\n   111\t    try:\n   112\t        yield\n   113\t    finally:\n   114\t        sweeper.cancel()\n   115\t        await pool.close()\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\tapp = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)\n   119\tapp.include_router(ingest.router)\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef authenticate(request: Request, creds: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials = Depends(bearer)) -> Principal:\n   123\t    settings = request.app.state.settings\n   124\t    try:\n   125\t        key = request.app.state.jwks.get_signing_key_from_jwt(creds.credentials)\n   126\t        claims = jwt.decode(\n   127\t            creds.credentials,\n   128\t            key.key,\n   129\t            algorithms=[\"RS256\", \"ES256\"],\n   130\t            audience=settings.oidc_audience,\n   131\t            issuer=settings.oidc_issuer,\n   132\t            options={\"require\": [\"exp\", \"iat\", \"sub\", \"aud\", \"iss\"]},\n   133\t        )\n   134\t    except jwt.PyJWTError as exc:\n   135\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"invalid token\") from exc\n   136\t    bu = claims.get(\"bu\")\n   137\t    if not bu:\n   138\t        raise HTTPException(403, \"token has no business unit\")\n   139\t    return Principal(subject=claims[\"sub\"], business_unit=bu)\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t@app.post(\"/runs\")\n   143\tasync def start_run(req: RunRequest, request: Request, principal: Principal = Depends(authenticate)) -> dict:\n   144\t    settings = request.app.state.settings\n   145\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n   146\t    trace_id = format(span_ctx.trace_id, \"032x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else uuid.uuid4().hex\n   147\t    ident = RunIdentity(\n   148\t        accountable_party=principal.subject,\n   149\t        operational_owner=settings.operational_owner,\n   150\t        tenant=principal.business_unit,\n   151\t        agent_type_id=request.app.state.agent_type_id,\n   152\t        agent_instance_id=new_instance_id(),\n   153\t        trace_id=trace_id,\n   154\t        run_id=f\"run-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n   155\t        delegated_subject=principal.subject,\n   156\t        agent_principal=AGENT_PRINCIPAL,\n   157\t    )\n   158\t    task = f\"Department: {req.department}\\n\\n{req.task}\"\n   159\t    asyncio.create_task(request.app.state.agent.run(ident, task))\n   160\t    return {\"run_id\": ident.run_id, \"agent_instance_id\": ident.agent_instance_id}\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t@app.post(\"/slack/interactions\")\n   164\tasync def slack_interactions(request: Request) -> dict:\n   165\t    body = await request.body()\n   166\t    timestamp = request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Request-Timestamp\", \"0\")\n   167\t    if abs(time.time() - int(timestamp)) > 300:\n   168\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"stale request\")\n   169\t    secret = Path(request.app.state.settings.slack_signing_secret_path).read_bytes().strip()\n   170\t    expected = \"v0=\" + hmac.new(secret, f\"v0:{timestamp}:\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n   171\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Signature\", \"\")):\n   172\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"bad signature\")\n   173\t\n   174\t    payload = json.loads(parse_qs(body.decode())[\"payload\"][0])\n   175\t    action = payload[\"actions\"][0]\n   176\t    slack_user = payload[\"user\"][\"id\"]\n   177\t    row = await request.app.state.pool.fetchrow(\n   178\t        \"SELECT email, role FROM approvers WHERE slack_user_id = $1 AND active\", slack_user\n   179\t    )\n   180\t    if row is None:\n   181\t        raise HTTPException(403, \"not an approver\")\n   182\t    try:\n   183\t        await request.app.state.approvals.decide(\n   184\t            action[\"value\"], approver=row[\"email\"], approver_role=row[\"role\"],\n   185\t            approve=action[\"action_id\"] == \"approve\",\n   186\t        )\n   187\t    except ApproverNotAuthorized as exc:\n   188\t        raise HTTPException(403, str(exc)) from exc\n   189\t    except ValueError as exc:\n   190\t        raise HTTPException(409, str(exc)) from exc\n   191\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t@app.get(\"/healthz\")\n   195\tasync def healthz() -> dict:\n   196\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n=== app/tools/erp.py\n     1\t\"\"\"ERP tools: budget lookups, generic ERP reads, and purchase-order creation.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\tfrom typing import Any\n     5\t\n     6\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n     7\tfrom app.tools import Tool\n     8\t\n     9\tERP_READ_SCOPE = \"erp.read\"\n    10\tERP_PO_WRITE_SCOPE = \"erp.read erp.po.create\"\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\tdef tools(deps) -> list[Tool]:\n    14\t    erp = deps.erp\n    15\t\n    16\t    async def get_budget(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n    17\t        return await erp.call(\n    18\t            \"budget.get_remaining\",\n    19\t            {\"business_unit\": ident.tenant, \"department\": args[\"department\"], \"fiscal_period\": args[\"fiscal_period\"]},\n    20\t            ident,\n    21\t            ERP_READ_SCOPE,\n    22\t        )\n    23\t\n    24\t    async def erp_call(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n    25\t        arguments = dict(args.get(\"arguments\", {}))\n    26\t        arguments[\"business_unit\"] = ident.tenant\n    27\t        return await erp.call(args[\"operation\"], arguments, ident, deps.erp_scope_for(args[\"operation\"]))\n    28\t\n    29\t    async def create_purchase_order(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n    30\t        return await erp.call(\n    31\t            \"po.create\",\n    32\t            {\n    33\t                \"business_unit\": ident.tenant,\n    34\t                \"department\": args[\"department\"],\n    35\t                \"vendor_id\": args[\"vendor_id\"],\n    36\t                \"lines\": args[\"lines\"],\n    37\t                \"currency\": args[\"currency\"],\n    38\t                \"source_doc_id\": args[\"source_doc_id\"],\n    39\t                \"client_reference\": args[\"source_doc_id\"],\n    40\t            },\n    41\t            ident,\n    42\t            ERP_PO_WRITE_SCOPE,\n    43\t        )\n    44\t\n    45\t    line_schema = {\n    46\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n    47\t        \"properties\": {\n    48\t            \"sku\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n    49\t            \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 256},\n    50\t            \"quantity\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0},\n    51\t            \"unit_price_cents\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0},\n    52\t        },\n    53\t        \"required\": [\"sku\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price_cents\"],\n    54\t        \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    55\t    }\n    56\t\n    57\t    return [\n    58\t        Tool(\n    59\t            name=\"get_budget\",\n    60\t            description=\"Remaining budget for a department in a fiscal period.\",\n    61\t            input_schema={\n    62\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n    63\t                \"properties\": {\n    64\t                    \"department\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n    65\t                    \"fiscal_period\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^FY[0-9]{4}-Q[1-4]$\"},\n    66\t                },\n    67\t                \"required\": [\"department\", \"fiscal_period\"],\n    68\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    69\t            },\n    70\t            invoke=get_budget,\n    71\t        ),\n    72\t        Tool(\n    73\t            name=\"erp_call\",\n    74\t            description=(\n    75\t                \"Look up ERP records (vendors, invoices, purchase orders, budgets). \"\n    76\t                \"operation is an ERP operation name such as vendor.get or invoice.list_open.\"\n    77\t            ),\n    78\t            input_schema={\n    79\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n    80\t                \"properties\": {\n    81\t                    \"operation\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n    82\t                    \"arguments\": {\"type\": \"object\"},\n    83\t                },\n    84\t                \"required\": [\"operation\"],\n    85\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    86\t            },\n    87\t            invoke=erp_call,\n    88\t        ),\n    89\t        Tool(\n    90\t            name=\"create_purchase_order\",\n    91\t            description=\"Raise a purchase order in the ERP for an approved quote.\",\n    92\t            input_schema={\n    93\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n    94\t                \"properties\": {\n    95\t                    \"department\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n    96\t                    \"vendor_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 32},\n    97\t                    \"currency\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^[A-Z]{3}$\"},\n    98\t                    \"source_doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n    99\t                    \"lines\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": line_schema, \"maxItems\": 200},\n   100\t                },\n   101\t                \"required\": [\"department\", \"vendor_id\", \"currency\", \"source_doc_id\", \"lines\"],\n   102\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   103\t            },\n   104\t            invoke=create_purchase_order,\n   105\t            target_field=\"source_doc_id\",\n   106\t        ),\n   107\t    ]\n=== migrations/001_init.sql\n     1\t-- Procurement agent schema. Applied by the migration job with the\n     2\t-- procurement_owner role; the running agent connects as procurement_agent.\n     3\t\n     4\tCREATE TABLE audit_events (\n     5\t    node_id             text PRIMARY KEY,\n     6\t    parent_node_id      text REFERENCES audit_events (node_id),\n     7\t    run_id              text NOT NULL,\n     8\t    ts                  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n     9\t    kind                text NOT NULL,\n    10\t    accountable_party   text NOT NULL CHECK (accountable_party <> ''),\n    11\t    operational_owner   text NOT NULL CHECK (operational_owner <> ''),\n    12\t    tenant              text NOT NULL CHECK (tenant <> ''),\n    13\t    agent_type_id       text NOT NULL CHECK (agent_type_id <> ''),\n    14\t    agent_instance_id   text NOT NULL CHECK (agent_instance_id <> ''),\n    15\t    trace_id            text NOT NULL CHECK (trace_id <> ''),\n    16\t    span_id             text,\n    17\t    delegated_subject   text NOT NULL,\n    18\t    agent_principal     text NOT NULL,\n    19\t    parent_instance_id  text,\n    20\t    policy_version      text,\n    21\t    approval_id         text,\n    22\t    operation_id        text,\n    23\t    context_tokens      integer CHECK (context_tokens IS NULL OR context_tokens > 0),\n    24\t    context_method      text NOT NULL,\n    25\t    context_compacted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    26\t    payload             jsonb NOT NULL\n    27\t);\n    28\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_run ON audit_events (run_id, ts);\n    29\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_instance ON audit_events (agent_instance_id, ts);\n    30\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_trace ON audit_events (trace_id);\n    31\t\n    32\tCREATE TABLE approvals (\n    33\t    id                     text PRIMARY KEY,\n    34\t    tool                   text NOT NULL,\n    35\t    target                 text NOT NULL,\n    36\t    args_sha256            text NOT NULL,\n    37\t    args_summary           jsonb NOT NULL,\n    38\t    tenant                 text NOT NULL,\n    39\t    requested_by_instance  text NOT NULL,\n    40\t    requested_by_run       text NOT NULL,\n    41\t    delegated_subject      text NOT NULL,\n    42\t    status                 text NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'approved', 'rejected', 'expired')),\n    43\t    requested_at           timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    44\t    expires_at             timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    45\t    approver               text,\n    46\t    approver_role          text,\n    47\t    decided_at             timestamptz\n    48\t);\n    49\tCREATE INDEX approvals_lookup ON approvals (tool, target, tenant, status);\n    50\t\n    51\tCREATE TABLE approvers (\n    52\t    slack_user_id  text PRIMARY KEY,\n    53\t    email          text NOT NULL,\n    54\t    role           text NOT NULL,\n    55\t    business_unit  text NOT NULL,\n    56\t    active         boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true\n    57\t);\n    58\t\n    59\tCREATE TABLE documents (\n    60\t    doc_id         text PRIMARY KEY,\n    61\t    business_unit  text NOT NULL,\n    62\t    source         text NOT NULL,\n    63\t    media_type     text NOT NULL,\n    64\t    sha256         text NOT NULL,\n    65\t    status         text NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('accepted', 'quarantined')),\n    66\t    reject_reason  text,\n    67\t    text           text,\n    68\t    received_at    timestamptz NOT NULL\n    69\t);\n    70\tCREATE INDEX documents_bu ON documents (business_unit, doc_id);\n    71\t\n    72\tCREATE TABLE dept_notes (\n    73\t    note_id            text PRIMARY KEY,\n    74\t    business_unit      text NOT NULL,\n    75\t    department         text NOT NULL,\n    76\t    kind               text NOT NULL,\n    77\t    body               text NOT NULL,\n    78\t    verified           boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n    79\t    verified_by        text,\n    80\t    quarantined        boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n    81\t    expires_at         timestamptz,\n    82\t    writer_instance    text NOT NULL,\n    83\t    writer_type_id     text NOT NULL,\n    84\t    run_id             text NOT NULL,\n    85\t    source_doc_id      text,\n    86\t    delegated_subject  text NOT NULL,\n    87\t    context_tokens     integer,\n    88\t    context_method     text NOT NULL,\n    89\t    created_at         timestamptz NOT NULL\n    90\t);\n    91\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_lookup ON dept_notes (business_unit, department, created_at DESC);\n    92\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_source ON dept_notes (source_doc_id);\n    93\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_writer ON dept_notes (writer_instance);\n    94\t\n    95\tCREATE TABLE control_flags (\n    96\t    scope    text PRIMARY KEY,           -- 'fleet' or 'tenant:<business_unit>'\n    97\t    halted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    98\t    reason   text NOT NULL,\n    99\t    set_by   text NOT NULL,\n   100\t    set_at   timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n   101\t);\n   102\t\n   103\tCREATE TABLE spend_quota (\n   104\t    scope      text NOT NULL,\n   105\t    key        text NOT NULL,\n   106\t    day        date NOT NULL,\n   107\t    spent_usd  numeric(12, 4) NOT NULL,\n   108\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, day)\n   109\t);\n   110\t\n   111\tCREATE TABLE run_start_window (\n   112\t    scope   text NOT NULL,\n   113\t    key     text NOT NULL,\n   114\t    minute  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n   115\t    starts  integer NOT NULL,\n   116\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, minute)\n   117\t);\n   118\t\n   119\t-- Runtime role: append-only audit, no access to control flags beyond reading.\n   120\tREVOKE ALL ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public FROM procurement_agent;\n   121\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;\n   122\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON approvals TO procurement_agent;\n   123\tGRANT SELECT ON approvers TO procurement_agent;\n   124\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON documents TO procurement_agent;\n   125\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON dept_notes TO procurement_agent;\n   126\tGRANT SELECT ON control_flags TO procurement_agent;\n   127\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON spend_quota TO procurement_agent;\n   128\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON run_start_window TO procurement_agent;\n   129\t\n   130\t-- Operators: halt and resume.\n   131\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control_flags TO procurement_ops;\n   132\tGRANT SELECT ON audit_events TO procurement_ops;\n   133\tGRANT SELECT, UPDATE (verified, verified_by, quarantined) ON dept_notes TO procurement_ops;\n=== README.md\n     1\t# procurement-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Architecture\n     9\t\n    10\t```\n    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n    22\t```\n    23\t\n    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Context size\n    43\t\n    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n    45\t\n    46\t| method | meaning |\n    47\t|---|---|\n    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n    51\t\n    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side tru","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-batch-flvfok0r/30aafd76-3534-4666-ab29-0933a8953e34/tool-results/byh98t99m.txt","persistedOutputSize":30743},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017F8D7Lk9xcMHcpVxSKnLn9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
