{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016iuG1fobv5UJH4B8tJycsm","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved C08.2 = yes. Next: C08.1 — Each trace or audit record carries the agent-type-id or manifest reference that resolves to the stored release manifest.\n  How to verify: 1) Open the trace or audit record writer. 2) Check every record carries `agent.type.id` or a manifest reference. 3) Check that value is the key of a stored manifest. 4) Answer no if the field is missing on some paths (errors, background jobs) or holds a value that resolves to no stored manifest.\nSaved C08.1 = no. Next: C08.3 — Prompts passed from a parent to a sub-agent are stored and linked from the trace.\n  How to verify: 1) Find sub-agent spawn code. 2) Check the parent's prompt is stored and the trace holds a link to it (ID, hash, or URI). 3) Answer no if the prompt is not stored, prompt capture is off, or the trace has no link.\nSaved C08.3 = no. Next: C08.4 — Storage config keeps manifests, traces, and these links for at least the audit retention period, and limits access to sensitive artifacts by role.\n  How to verify: 1) Find storage config for manifests, traces, and prompt links: bucket lifecycle rules, log retention, TTLs. 2) Check retention covers the audit period for all of them. 3) Check IAM limits sensitive artifacts by role. 4) Answer no if any has a shorter TTL, no retention, or broad read access. Answer unknown if storage is configured outside this repo.\nSaved C08.4 = unknown. Next: finish item C08 with `answer.py ... item C08 --rating ...`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30aafd76-3534-4666-ab29-0933a8953e34","uuid":"33b64b94-d3f9-4f0c-a800-cbcbf97f7f03","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:28:39.432Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved C08.2 = yes. Next: C08.1 — Each trace or audit record carries the agent-type-id or manifest reference that resolves to the stored release manifest.\n  How to verify: 1) Open the trace or audit rec