{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZzJnH2zYf8ebwsJf5f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C08, E01, E02, E03 and E04, and all five are rated `gap`. `agent/brace-findings.json` is saved and passes the `--batch C08,E01,E02,E03,E04 --before-challenges` validation. I did not run challenges or add any other items.\n\n- **C08:** Audit rows carry `agent_type_id` and the context size on both model paths (`app/loop.py:154`, `app/extractor.py:78`), so C08.2 is `yes`.\n  - C08.1 is `no`. The id is a one-way hash, and no stored manifest is keyed by it (`app/identity.py:68`). The hash covers prompt paths, not prompt contents.\n  - C08.3 is `no`. The sub-agent \"prompt ref\" is only a span id (`app/extractor.py:58`), and the task text is never stored.\n  - C08.4 is `unknown`. I found no retention or lifecycle config in the repo.\n- **E01:** There is no inventory file. The manifest lists only the ERP MCP server, with a single owner (`release/manifest.yaml:63-66`). The payments API, Slack proxy, STS, OIDC, egress proxy, OTel collector and Anthropic API are missing. All three checks are `no`.\n- **E02:** Only direct dependencies are pinned. There is no lockfile or hash check (`Dockerfile:7`), no dependency signature verification, no vulnerability scan in CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`), and no approval records. All four checks are `no`.\n- **E03:** Tool fingerprints are compared only at startup (`app/mcp_client.py:95-98`).\n  - `refresh_tools` replaces the tool set with no compare (`app/mcp_client.py:107-111`), so newly discovered tools are enabled immediately.\n  - The `list_changed` handler is never wired to anything.\n  - There is no implementation pin, no quarantine and no config propagation bound. All five checks are `no`.\n- **E04:** The scanner runs only at startup, not on refresh.\n  - It has no data-sending-target rule.\n  - Its cross-tool and role-override rules are very narrow, and `json.dumps` escapes control characters before the regexes run.\n  - The length limit covers only descriptions.\n  - Server instructions, prompt templates and resource templates are never fetched or scanned. All four checks are `no`.\n\n- **Prescan hits:** The 7 hits all belong to B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05, so none apply to this batch. I left them unresolved.\n- **Shared evidence:** The validator flagged shared failing lines between E03/E04 and E01/E02. I moved the E04.3, E04.4 and E02.4 evidence to different lines rather than adding `also_affects`.\n- **E04 applicability:** The ERP tool metadata is never shown to the model, because `erp_call` uses an in-house schema (`app/tools/erp.py`). The N/A condition for E04 does not clearly hold, since the client does load MCP tools, so I rated against the checks as written.\n- **Review notes:** I filled in `scope` by editing the JSON directly, since `answer.py` has no command for it. The reasoning setting was not recorded."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_read_input_tokens":80562,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640},"output_tokens":786,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30aafd76-3534-4666-ab29-0933a8953e34","uuid":"b0bbab1f-6977-4b58-ba4e-a7b11a9741c3","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:29:43.818Z","request_id":"req_011CgDZzJUvEsJP4BVp9p6Ki"}
